Finite bodies, eigenmodes and transient superposition (@th-eigenmodes: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer, #source "../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD", #source "../sources/Second-Level-Heat-Transfer-Vedula.lingua#r_663BY2CF56BBB35C1S595A2VRF", #source "../sources/Differential-Equations-MIT-18-03SC.lingua#r_1VJHPM3DQ0PWYNFYKD11EKGCZE", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "Time-dependent-boundaries-Duhamel-and-thermal-networks.lingua#r_5HXNCTPBZKN5QHF2EMAW2TZ5W4") { r_1322FT380D62ASTAD04KKTC8G8
**Read:** [A Heat Transfer Textbook — Lienhard and Lienhard](../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD), finite-body transient conduction; [Second Level Course in Heat Transfer — R. P. Vedula](../sources/Second-Level-Heat-Transfer-Vedula.lingua#r_663BY2CF56BBB35C1S595A2VRF), orthogonality and higher-dimensional extensions; [Differential Equations — MIT 18.03SC](../sources/Differential-Equations-MIT-18-03SC.lingua#r_1VJHPM3DQ0PWYNFYKD11EKGCZE), Fourier series and systems.

Finite-body conduction depends on geometry, boundary conditions and the initial field. Separate variables where justified, derive the eigenvalue condition and expand the initial state in the appropriate orthogonal modes. The coefficients encode the actual initial distribution.

Compare a full series with a first-mode approximation over a declared time range. Early-time boundary layers may require many modes even when a late-time exponential fits well. Centre, surface and average temperatures have different series weights.

Derive a slab solution and verify spatial/time limits, integrated energy and dimensional scaling. Use complete relevant mathematical sections rather than treating a chart as an unexplained oracle. Compare the continuum solution with [An inspectable conservative transient layered slab](../computation/An-inspectable-conservative-transient-layered-slab.lingua#r_6B5B7E7C3Z1APY0RYAC09P12ET) under the same boundary and initial conditions.

